{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40793-crossover-mechanics","id":40793,"title":"Crossover mechanics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T16:17:28-08:00","id":40793,"title":"Crossover mechanics?","content":"When the various entities of the World of Darkness are dealing with one another, I'm wondering what all stats would be needed to be added for cross-relation.<br /> As an example, from Vampire, there are many points in the game where you need to check versus an opponents virtues or humanity, such as with Dementation. Virtues and Humanity, however, are not a standard part of character creation for the other games, and would need added in for crossovers.<br /> <br /> My question is, other than Vampire Virtues, what all other stats would need to be made universal if you had a room full of all of the WoD entities?<br /> <br /> {please do not bog down this thread with other crossover advice / complaints}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T18:13:56-08:00","id":40856,"title":"","content":"That just amounts to all of the different Traits floating around on character sheets, right?<br /> <br /> Vampire: Generation is also a concern, possibly. It is a Trait that Vampires have, but i'm not familiar enough with them to know if any powers or other systems refer to it or depend on it for any effects.<br /> <br /> From the Werewolf corner: Rage, Gnosis, Rank, Renown; Ananasi and Nuwisha omit Rage, Nagah omit Renown. Spirits will also have Essence (formerly Power).<br /> <br /> Spirit-Possessed (fomori, drones, etc.): possibly Rage and/or Gnosis. Types other than Kami have Autonomy.<br /> <br /> From Mage: Arete, Quintessence, Paradox, Resonance<br /> <br /> Wraith: Pathos, Passions (both Psyche and Shadow), Fetters, Angst/Psyche, Passions<br /> <br /> Changeling: Glamour, Banality<br /> <br /> Hunter: Virtues (different set), Conviction<br /> <br /> Demon: Faith, Torment<br /> <br /> Mummy (old type): Virtues (also a different set), Sekhem, Ba, Ka<br /> <br /> Mummy (Amenti): Balance, Sekhem<br /> <br /> Inquisitors: Basic and Advanced Virtue Types, Conviction<br /> <br /> (KotE Traits omitted because it already tells you exactly what equals what between Gui Ren and Kindred in the book)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-01-2014, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T23:31:15-08:00","id":40940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40793-crossover-mechanics?p=40856#post40856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just amounts to all of the different Traits floating around on character sheets, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than that. It's the question of which of those traits are relevant in some way beyond the internal.<br /> <br /> For example: the Vampire Virtue of Courage still gets called into question when certain panic-inducing abilities are used. Even mortals are supposed to make a Courage roll, or else be sent into a state of fear like the Red Fear against some of these abilities. A stat that doesn't appear outside of Vampire. Similarly, several Discipline powers set their difficulty based on the opponent's Humanity. (Daimonion &amp; Dementation come immediately to mind)<br /> Conversely, the only common external instance where someone other than you uses your Generation stat is the fact that Dominate doesn't work on a kindred who is of higher generation. In that case, and the few others where the stat comes up: if you aren't a kindred, then the point is moot.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, to use some of the items on your list that I am familiar with, to help me clarify:<br /> Gnosis, the only times that this could come up from an external perspective the rules mention how to handle it. Whether the power doesn't affect people who don't have Gnosis or affects them differently, or requires Willpower instead.<br /> \u200bGorgons Autonomy stat is purely internal. No external factor adjusts this, it is purely a gauge of factors for the character himself.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you had a purely mundane mortal who would have to deal with each of the various supernaturals of the WoD, and upon meeting them they would be using the stats and abilities of their game rules, what all stats would you need other than just the Abilities, Attributes, and Willpower. And, apparently, Vampire Virtues / Humanity system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T23:52:48-08:00","id":40948,"title":"","content":"I think Saur got it in one. The tricky thing is, all of these individual stats are relevant to that supernatural being and they are not universally compatible by the nature of what they belong to. I know you're asking if it's possible to just either have one name for the stat across all systems, but I don't think it's that simple to call whatever power a supernatural has as just the Juice rating and be done with it. The differences in Blood pool/Gnosis/Quintessence/Pathos/Glamor/Virtue etc are what set each of those beings apart. By the rules themselves each power is not equivalent to the other. For example 1 blood point from a werewolf counts for 2 to a Vampire because of its potency compared with human blood. So a Mage's blood would still be only one point to a Vampire unless perhaps the mage happened to be Kinfolk. And Changeling blood counts for 1 point but brings automatic Dementia to the imbibing Vampire. Or how bout changeling Glamour being more potent than Mage Quintessence? If the fae are raw magic in a human shell, their powers are closer to the surface. Magi channel power in a limited structured sense by comparison. It's these comparisons and diversities in figuring out how to cross the systems that make it so interesting and incredibly frustrating at the same time. But giving it universal rules and terms across systems for what makes each supernatural unique will either wind up more frustrating since the rules don't support the equity or it'll take away some of the uniqueness of that being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:22:13-08:00","id":40955,"title":"","content":"@ D_R:<br /> That's not what I'm trying to do / figure out.<br /> \u200bIn a hypothetical room that had all of the supernaturals in it, and a normal human, what stats would need to be added to that human under each of the various systems.<br /> He would need Courage, because of Daimonion and other Disciplines. He would need Humanity, because of Dementation, and other Disciplines.<br /> He would not need Gnosis, because that would not be called into question for him.<br /> He does not need Arete, Quintessence, Paradox, Resonance, Rage, Rank, Renown, Autonomy, and so on for the same reason.<br /> He has a blood pool, which is normally at 10, but he can't use it, and loosing it can cause damage.<br /> He might have Mana, but unless he learns Linear Magic, Psycic abilities, or certain Numen, he can't use it, and thus it does not matter what the rating is.<br /> <br /> Basically, I am familiar with the mechanics of the &quot;Big three&quot; of WoD, but not enough with the other titles rules. Vampire assumes that everything sentient has its Virtues, and builds abilities around that assumption. Mage and Werewolf do not do so, in fact assuming that only Mages have Mage stats, and only Werewolves have Werewolf stats.<br /> I've never played Wraith. I know nothing about Wraith. I have no idea if mook humans, or other supernaturals, are assumed to have some set of stats or another under Wraith rules.<br /> <br /> To Emphasis my response: I am not trying to make anything equal another thing; I am not trying to have a Vampire with Gnosis (*cringe*); I am trying to figure out what the rule systems I am unfamiliar with <i>assumes <b>everyone</b> has</i>, and thus would need to <b>actually have</b> in <b>order to interact</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:37:49-08:00","id":40961,"title":"","content":"Most of the games are structured like WtA and MtA: they assume that mortals don't have supernatural specific traits, so they make sure powers that can apply to other beings (humans or other supernaturals) rely on the common traits like Attributes or Willpower.<br /> <br /> VtM is the only game that really assumes that everything has VtM Virtues and Humanity/Path ratings (keeping in mind that, in RAW canon, humans do have those traits).<br /> <br /> This isn't perfect, but with all the game-lines that stack up in the cWOD, a few powers falling through the cracks here and there are expected to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T03:51:37-08:00","id":41014,"title":"","content":"Check out Mr. Gone's character sheets. I believe there's one in there just for a mortal. It basically has all the stats you're talking about but no blood pool. (Called health levels for everyone else starting out mortal, losing blood is part of damage unless you just want to calculate how much a Vampire is taking) I think it might have Humanity as it was adjusted from a ghoul character sheet originally. There could even be a version you can format yourself to add or take out traits to update it for a 20th system rules set. Hope it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T04:09:22-08:00","id":41019,"title":"","content":"Actually, if you check the Antagonist Chapters of the major game lines, they <i>do</i> apply all that game's traits to the other species. In Werewolf, the example vampires have Gnosis and Rage. Each game has its own view of the WoD that doesn't take into account any other game. When running a crossover chronicle, it's up to the ST to decide how to manage that dissonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T08:55:17-08:00","id":41139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40793-crossover-mechanics?p=41014#post41014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might have Humanity as it was adjusted from a ghoul character sheet originally.</div> </div> </div> </div>While possible, books like WOD: Mafia use Humanity for mortal characters with no supernatural connections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40793-crossover-mechanics?p=41019#post41019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if you check the Antagonist Chapters of the major game lines, they <i>do</i> apply all that game's traits to the other species.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also quite clearly (and often explicitly) just a short-cut for modelling powers so you don't have to buy other books to have various supernaturals in your game. WtA leeches don't have the mystical trait of Rage. The game uses Rage to model things like Celerity so you don't have to buy VtM to stat up vampires.<br /> <br /> And it's also somewhat irrelevant considering that the thread is explicitly about crossover rules in the first place and which game lines produce significant powers that could conceivably be used on other supernaturals but uses traits those targets don't have.<br /> <br /> ZhyzhaksMate is explicitly asking for which powers in other game-lines would create dissonance such as a Discipline that uses Humanity as the base difficulty being used on a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T06:14:31-08:00","id":46203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40793-crossover-mechanics?p=41014#post41014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out Mr. Gone's character sheets. I believe there's one in there just for a mortal. It basically has all the stats you're talking about but no blood pool. (Called health levels for everyone else starting out mortal, losing blood is part of damage unless you just want to calculate how much a Vampire is taking) I think it might have Humanity as it was adjusted from a ghoul character sheet originally. There could even be a version you can format yourself to add or take out traits to update it for a 20th system rules set. Hope it helps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, I have both a Mortals and a Ghoul sheet. I even have some updated for V20 rules. I might even have a few mortal sheets for some of the various game lines...<br /> <br /> I've tried a few times to make a &quot;catch-all&quot; or generic sheet for CWoD like I have for NWoD, but theres too many different traits between the supernaturals to make it work right, sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T07:17:46-08:00","id":46237,"title":"","content":"I remember that the &quot;default&quot; virtues for a Mage/Sorcerer, for cross-over purposes w/Vampire, were Conscience:2, Self-Control:3 and Courage:5, with the caveat that individual mages may vary by one or two points. Otherwise, I/my friends always used the suggested Dif.6 default for cross-over difficulties (not anywhere near my books, so I can't look it up just now, but I remember this being brought up umpteen times back in the 90's and 00's in various incarnations of the old forums and the Powers That Be suggested that as a good median.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}